<description>
**Problem:** Nodes that synced before v28 may store block and undo files effectively unobfuscated with a zero XOR key. There is no built-in way to obfuscate those existing files, rotate their key, or deliberately replace it with a zero key without resyncing.

**Fix:** Add `-reobfuscate-blocks[=<value>]` to rewrite existing `blk*.dat` and `rev*.dat` files before chainstate loading. With no value or `=1`, the option generates a random 8-byte key. A 16-character hexadecimal value selects an exact key, including all zeros to remove obfuscation, while malformed values fail during startup. If the selected key is already active, block and undo files are left unchanged.

Files are rewritten in fixed-size chunks, staged with a `.reobfuscated` suffix, committed before the originals are removed, and renamed to their original names after all rewrites finish. The target key is staged as `xor.dat.reobfuscated`, which is also used to resume an interrupted migration. File modification times are preserved, and progress is reported in the log and through kernel notifications marked as resumable.

**Benchmark:** The migration is single-threaded and processes one file at a time.

| CPU | Storage | Block count | Size | Files | Time (min) | Blocks/min |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Apple M4 Max laptop | SSD | ~955k | ~854 GB | 11,232 | 10.18 | 93,804 |
| Intel Core i9 | SSD | ~909k | ~725 GB | 10,238 | 23.1 | 39,351 |
| Raspberry Pi 5 | SSD | ~914k | ~728 GB | 10,276 | 72.78 | 12,558 |
| Intel Core i7 | HDD | ~909k | ~720 GB | 10,156 | 208.7 | 4,356 |
| Raspberry Pi 4B | HDD | ~915k | ~730 GB | 10,304 | 1467 | 624 |

**Similar work:**

- [contrib: add xor-blocks tool to obfuscate blocks directory #32451](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/32451)
- [andrewtoth/blocks-xor](https://github.com/andrewtoth/blocks-xor)
</description>

<commits>
3f0c1f93f4 index: remove always-false obfuscation parameter

All `BaseIndex::DB` callers leave database obfuscation disabled, and the only explicit argument is `false`.
Remove the parameter and rely on the `DBParams` default.

f390057c18 refactor: add `Obfuscation` key helpers

Name the fixed-size key type and add helpers for parsing keys and deriving the XOR delta between keys.
This keeps the block reobfuscation commit focused on file migration.

4c0fbf9e6b refactor: extract XOR key file helpers

Centralize `xor.dat` reading and creation so block reobfuscation can reuse the serialization and close-error handling.

797f66d99c node: commit XOR keys before closing files

Commit newly written XOR keys before closing the file so they are durable before migration can remove data encoded under the old key.
This also commits keys created during normal block-storage initialization.

44034d0b33 util: report directory commit failures

Return and log directory-sync failures so block migration can stop before removing or activating files whose directory changes are not durable.
Existing callers may continue to ignore the result.

8f4640abf5 refactor: extract block and undo file discovery

Extract `blk` and `rev` discovery from `CleanupBlockRevFiles` so block reobfuscation can share a directory scan that handles gaps left by pruning.

aea6334fd6 node: log when block file XOR is inactive

Suggest `-reobfuscate-blocks` when the key is zero and block-file XOR is enabled.
Suppress the suggestion for `-blocksxor=0`, which explicitly leaves the files unobfuscated.

Co-authored-by: sedited <seb.kung@gmail.com>

9baf6defd9 blocks: reobfuscate block and undo files

Rewrite existing block and undo files under a requested or random XOR key.
Stage the target key before rewriting files, and commit each replacement before removing its original so interrupted migrations can resume safely.
Collect staged replacements before activating them, and return without staging when the requested key is already active.
Reject direct block-storage access until a pending migration has finished, so it cannot recreate the missing XOR key.
Keep new modification times so size-and-mtime backups copy rewritten files along with the new XOR key.

Co-authored-by: Anthony Towns <aj@erisian.com.au>

f46005285f init: add block file reobfuscation option

Add `-reobfuscate-blocks` and run the requested or pending migration before chainstate loading.
Accept random or exact keys and reject malformed values.
Require a zero target with `-blocksxor=0`, including when resuming a pending migration.
Report the migration in RPC warmup status.
Report migration exceptions as initialization errors so filesystem failures retain their details instead of escaping startup.

Co-authored-by: sedited <seb.kung@gmail.com>

eb5d79a53a test: cover block file reobfuscation

Cover key selection and validation, same-key reruns, and resume before copying, from partial copies, and during file activation.
Exercise removal of obfuscation and resuming a zero-key migration with `-blocksxor=0`.

52f21d7548 node: report block reobfuscation progress

Report block reobfuscation through `kernel::Notifications` so GUI users can follow the long-running startup operation.
Set `resume_possible` because a restart continues from `xor.dat.reobfuscated`.

Co-authored-by: Ryan Ofsky <ryan@ofsky.org>
Co-authored-by: sedited <seb.kung@gmail.com>

ec31cf7222 doc: describe block file reobfuscation
